{"kind":"stack","id":"s-mix","title":"Separating mixtures: solids, liquids and gases","theme":{"background":"#f4f9f4","foreground":"#1d3b1d","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"sun"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"Sand and water are mixed. Which way would separate the sand from the water?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"Filtering","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Magnetism","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"Colouring","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"Which tool would you use to separate large stones from small gravel?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"Sieve","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Magnet","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"Sieve with larger holes","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-t","content":"Evaporation"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-e","content":"Heat turns a liquid into a gas, leaving the solid behind. Salt is left when salt water dries out."},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"You have a cup of muddy water. Your teacher asks you to clean it. What do you do first?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Pour it through filter paper","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4a"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Leave it in the sun to dry out","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4b"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4a","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4a-t","content":"The filter catches the mud. Clear water drips into the cup. Well done."},{"type":"button","id":"c4a-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4b","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4b-t","content":"The water evaporates, but the mud stays behind in the cup. The water is lost, so try filtering next time."},{"type":"button","id":"c4b-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"A mixture of salt and water is heated until the water disappears. What is left in the pan?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Salt","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"Nothing at all","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Sieving"},{"type":"text","id":"c6-e","content":"Shaking a mixture through a mesh so small pieces fall through and big pieces stay on top."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"Which mixture could you separate by filtering?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"Salt dissolved in water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Sand mixed with water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-c","label":"Air mixed with oxygen","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Which state of matter can pass through filter paper?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Solid","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Liquid","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Gas","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"You finished the mixtures quiz!"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-m","content":"You now know how solids, liquids and gases help us separate mixtures. Great work."}],"actions":[]}}
